<title>USA: NASD seen voting on mandating arbitration -WSJ.</title>
<headline>NASD seen voting on mandating arbitration -WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Securities Dealers is expected to vote Thursday to stop mandating arbitration of discrimination and harassment complaints on Wall Street, the Wall Street Journal reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The securities industry requires that anyone seeking a license to sell securities waive the right to sue his or her employer in court for alleged discrimination or sexual harassment, the paper said.</p>
<p>Pending discrimination suits against Merrill Lynch and Smith Barney, however, have prompted a push for changes in the mandatory arbitration rules, the paper added.</p>
</text>
